/** Sheet endpoints. The signed-in user's name comes in the X-User header. */
@RestController
@Validated
@RequestMapping("/api/sheets")
public class SheetController {

    /** A sheet as the screen shows it: its today, its clerk limit (two decimals; none for no limit) and
     *  its floor (two decimals), its terms (days), its late percent (two decimals) and its policy date (none: the sheet's today) and its period numbering from-date (none: off), the terms of each grade that has its own, and its cap (two decimals; none for no cap), and its proof threshold (two decimals; none for no threshold), and its note threshold (two decimals; none for no threshold), and its review threshold (two decimals; none for no threshold), and its grace days (none: off), and whether it is archived, and its entry date (none: off), and the number of its last settle batch (none before the first), and its pot (two decimals; none for no pot), and its parent sheet's id (none for no parent), and its fiscal start month (1 to 12), and its alert threshold (two decimals; none for off), and its rounding mode (half-up or half-even; none: by the policy date), and its escalation gap (days; none: off), and its review SLA (days; none: none), and its proof kinds (comma separated; none: none), and its default grade (none: A), and its mid and high score thresholds (none: no bands), and whether its score log is on, and its maximum of open claims per person (none: none), and its retired grades (in the order retired), and its grades (A, B and C, then those added in the order added), and its policy versions' from-dates in the order made (none: counts always).
     *  The dated settings show the value in force on the sheet's today; every value recorded for them is in
     *  settings. */
